## Constraints inherited

See `ops/rules.constraints.hybrid`. Slice-8a reinforcements:

- All foreign supplier identities come from `ops/companies.synthetic.hybrid` (HydroBayern · AutoComp etc are already listed there). Add new ones only if needed and only with ONRC/equivalent check + Ɛ-swap. The Meridian counterparty roster is largely complete from 2026-05-10.
- English correspondence still uses Ɛ in foreign IDs (DE USt-IdNr · TR Vergi No · CN USCC · IT P.IVA) per the safety convention. The Ɛ is universal across languages.
- Romanian docs remain Romanian (Diligent · AutoComp · intra-Meridian). No translation drift.
- Tone applies to all Romanian and English copy: no revolutionary/transformation language. International invoices and legal-sounding docs can be formal, but never marketing-flavored.
- Public site copy in `/about` (the new Meridian disclosure paragraph) follows §Tone — calm, concrete, honest.
- No new runtime prompts. Existing classifier/summarizer/invoice_extractor/contract_reviewer/ask/draft prompts handle the new content. If a prompt clearly fails on English input, that's an open edge — record it; do not silently amend the prompt mid-slice.
- No Send button. No autonomous email. (Trust principle.)
- DocumentIndexer is normal-analyzer registered (slice-5 framework) — Meridian docs flow through it without special-casing.

