    - Walk every line of §Acceptance · capture pass/fail
    - Manual: visit /app/inbox · verify 18 Atelier Nova docs unchanged · no Meridian rows visible
    - Manual: visit /about · verify Meridian disclosure paragraph reads naturally in RO
    - Manual: hit /api/ask with "Cine este furnizorul nostru pentru pompe hidraulice?" · verify HydroBayern cited
    - Tone check on the /about Meridian paragraph: read aloud · strip any slop
    - Build: cd apps/web && npm run check && npm run build

11. SHIP.
    - Append ONE PATCHLOG line to ops/slice-8a.meridian-foundation-bavaria.hybrid (timestamp · model · summary · doc-count actual per category · classifier agreement rate · any new open edges)
    - Update state in slice-8a frontmatter forming → stable
    - Append ONE PATCHLOG line to ops/project.state.hybrid · update §Now (current → slice-8b) · §Slices (slice-8 splits into 8a stable + 8b forming/seed)
    - Update CLAUDE.md §Common operations: generate-demo-pdfs --company meridian · seed_demo --company meridian
    - Final commit: "slice-8a: Meridian foundation + Linia Bavaria · 15 multilingual docs · state→stable"

Hard rules (do not violate):
- all identities from ops/companies.synthetic.hybrid · new counterparties added there FIRST (none expected in 8a)
- Ɛ-swap preserved in all CUI/IBAN/phone/J-number/USt-IdNr/Vergi-No/USCC/P.IVA values
- foreign correspondence in English · RO clients + intra-Meridian in Romanian · NO translation drift
- Meridian docs do NOT appear in /app/inbox visually · /api default filter handles this
- public site shows ONLY Atelier Nova as the visitor-facing inbox demo · Meridian is disclosed in /about as backstage
- no Send button anywhere · ever
- no new runtime prompts · existing classifier/summarizer/etc handle EN as best they can · record open edges
- if classifier disagrees with declared category for >2 of 15 docs: inspect each · YAML adjusts if doc is genuinely ambiguous · LLM wrong otherwise · log in patchlog · do NOT relax prompts

If invoice_extractor fails on HydroBayern EN invoices:
- the prompt was authored RO-first in slice-3 · it may need EN tolerance · record in OPEN EDGES · do not amend mid-slice · 8b or dedicated tuning slice handles it
- the slice still ships if classifier and summarizer work and invoice_extractor degrades gracefully (status="done" with partial extraction is acceptable for slice-8a; pure crash is not)

If a Meridian counterparty needs a person/email not in companies.synthetic:
- add to that file FIRST with Ɛ-swap and ONRC check (or equivalent for foreign entities — verify against the country's registry)
- commit the companies.synthetic update separately before the YAML that uses it

Confirm the plan in 3 lines, then start with task 1.
